- The code did not compile on Ubuntu 22.04 due to two distinct problems : the inclusion of a header that was misspelled and some problematic definition of PI. Some typos were fixed in the whole code.
- The code was previously using the lower left corner of the voxel to compute both normal vector and then volume fraction and has been switched to a centerwise definition in a consistent way : these volume fractions are displayed in 'vf.txt'. An estimate of the scatterer volume based on the volume fraction error, is performed (printed in logfile) : this also needs to be added to master branch for comparison. Please note that volume correction should remain disabled in WD for now.
- For the polarizability calculation, it seems that there was some flaws in the self-term dyadic calculation (inconsistency in the solid angle calculation and misplaced normalization of plane coefficients) that are now corrected. A simple domain assignment (position of the voxel VS position of the boundary) is taken into account in the polarizability calculation. It is now working only for Clausius-Mossotti prescription (so that M=0). All the quantities that correspond to the overall WD scheme are stored in 'WD.txt' (this may take some time).
- Polarizability tensor is symmetrized as required by iterative solvers (may introduce some asymmetry errors for some cases : not in vacuum). It can be expressed using either Cholesky-like decomposition coupled with Takagi factorization from which the matrix square root is determined or just the principal square root (Sylvester's formula). A timer is added so that these operations on matrices are tracked in time. These matrices can be accessed in 'polarizability.txt'.
- The code now works only with Draine's formulation of absorption cross-section (depends on polarizability tensors) and the optical theorem seems satisfied (from comparison of Cext-Cabs with integration over angles for Csca). These absorption cross-section values are printed to 'draine.txt'.
- The DDA system solved using Takagi decomposition has been modified : transpose operators were swapped on two steps of the matrix-vector products and two steps of the iterative solver process. It has also been solved using the principal square root formulation (no need to transpose) and compared to the above modifications : some small differences remain noticable.

All the quantities detailled from the plane coefficients to square root of polarizability tensor are computed in an attached Mathematica script. Moreover, printing WD quantities (volume fraction, polarizability tensors....) to file is enabled from print_wd in param.c. If printing is disabled, it is expected that it will take less time to run : there are no significant differences in processing time between both TD and WD.
